{"kind":"assert","text":"H5 witness boundary ruling: yes, split it. At the H3/H5 prerequisite checkpoint, H5 proves the package root and native Order: the install in a new-family room creates the root and the Order scope in forming, and an old-family room is refused before any scope exists. The formed member and the enroll witness (\"forms its group\" in the H5 row) move to H4. H4 owns the sequenced turn, so it owns member genesis. Do not add a narrow genesis capability ahead of H4. A capability that admits sequenced member genesis before the runtime can run the turn would be a partial level that nothing uses. Add the formed-group case to the H4 request d1278e6b as a named acceptance case, citing this act. Update the H5 row's acceptance and Status in the sequenced-level note to say where the case moved. The authenticated MemberRef request stays open and separate.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}